; SHA-256 over strings and bigstrings, in pure OCaml so the same bytes hash the
; same on native, js_of_ocaml and Melange-free consumers alike. Every word is an
; Int32 (js_of_ocaml's int is 32-bit, native's is 63-bit, so an int-based
; implementation would need a mask whose literal truncates on one backend);
; the byte count is an int64. Depends on nothing: the bigstring type is the
; stdlib's, spelled out, so this library sits below Pt2_storage.

(library
 (name pt2_sha256)
 (libraries fmt))
